  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 311 AM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nLingering light rain showers are expected Monday night into early \nTuesday morning across the eastern half of the region. This is \nthanks to the upper low weakening and slowly exiting the region. As \nthis system exits, the weather pattern becomes more benign beginning \non Tuesday lasting through the rest of the work week. Weak ridging \naloft will promote warmer and dry conditions areawide. Highs each \nday are forecast in the mid 60s to mid 70s for most locations. Lows \nlook to remain near to slightly above normal (mainly in the 40s) \nwhich will prolong the first frost date for many areas in the \nmeantime. Guidance has another upper-level disturbance approaching \nthe region by next weekend, favoring another potential setup for \nrain/storms. There remains quite a bit of disagreement amongst \nmodels of the track, positioning, and strength of the system. \nTherefore, details will become clearer in the coming days. \n\nLamberson",
